        "research": {
            "topic": "Cross-model AI review loops: using Codex to grade Claude's work (and vice versa)",
            "summary": "The 'claudex-loop' pattern is a Claude Code skill that hands Claude's plan and code to OpenAI's Codex for adversarial review, on the rule that whoever built it never grades it. Peer-reviewed research backs the premise: LLMs struggle to self-correct without external feedback and demonstrably favor their own outputs when acting as judge.",
