            "keyPoints": [
                "The core rule of the loop: whoever wrote it never grades it — Claude's plan goes to Codex, Codex's code comes back to Claude.",
                "This is a real, documented failure mode: LLMs often can't fix their own reasoning without outside feedback, and sometimes get worse trying.",
                "LLM judges recognize their own writing and score it higher than human raters do — measured at NeurIPS 2024.",
                "Codex CLI is open source under Apache-2.0 and runs locally in the terminal, so a second-opinion loop needs no extra infrastructure.",
                "Claude Code skills are just SKILL.md files; Anthropic made the Agent Skills format an open standard in December 2025.",
                "Review happens at the plan stage, before code exists — the cheapest place to kill a design flaw.",
                "Adoption is at 90% while trust keeps dropping — cross-model review targets exactly that gap."
            ],
